.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
target/
out/
.crush/
.serena/
.tipsy-config/
.target-sandbox/
.cargo/
# The wasm-bindgen output `cargo run -p xtask -- dist` writes: a build artifact, never committed.
# Root-anchored on purpose, so a `git add -A` can never commit a wasm bundle.
/web/dist/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.log
.superpowers/
web/vendor/*
!web/vendor/README.md
# The screen recordings the README's browser and web-terminal pictures are cut from: raw footage, too
# heavy for the history. The SVGs `cargo run -p xtask -- shots` writes are committed; these are not.
/docs/images/raw/
# The working notes, out of the published repository on purpose: `CLAUDE.md` is the agent's own
# instruction file (budget, environment traps, a queue of pending requests) and `docs/superpowers/` is
# the record of how each phase was planned and reviewed. Both stay on this machine and both are
# ignored rather than tracked, so a `git add -A` cannot put them back.
/CLAUDE.md
/docs/superpowers/
